  "published": "2026-11-18",
  "updated": "2026-11-18",
  "intro": "The primary alternatives to Empower are Monarch Money, YNAB, Quicken Simplifi, Betterment, Wealthfront and Fidelity Go. At The Modern Wallet, we evaluate personal finance tools and show the fee arithmetic so you can see whether a free dashboard, a paid budgeting subscription or an automated investment advisory account fits your goals.\n\n[Empower](https://www.empower.com/) divides its platform into two parts: free personal wealth tools and paid wealth management. The free tools cover net worth tracking, a retirement planner, portfolio analysis and budgeting. Its paid wealth management begins at $100,000 for Personal Strategy and $1,000,000 for Private Client, with advisory fees calculated on assets managed as disclosed in its Form ADV rather than published as a flat rate on its public pages. For cash, Empower Personal Cash offers a 3.50% Annual Percentage Yield (APY) with up to $5 million in Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) coverage.\n\nBecause Empower combines investment management with financial tracking, your choice depends on whether you need budgeting software or an investment manager. For deeper breakdowns in each category, see our [Monarch Money alternatives](/alternatives/monarch-money/) comparison, our [YNAB alternatives](/alternatives/ynab/) guide, our [Wealthfront alternatives](/alternatives/wealthfront/) review, our [Quicken alternatives](/alternatives/quicken/) overview, and our [financial product comparison hub](/compare/).",
